{
  "_README": [
    "Development fixture for the local Convex deployment. Loaded by `bun run seed:dev`.",
    "This file is CONTENT, not code - regenerate it freely, by hand or with a model, whenever the screens need a different shape of data.",
    "Numbers are synthetic on purpose: every one sits in a reserved-looking block so a fixture can never collide with a number a real person holds. They are still valid Indian mobile format, so normalisation and validation behave exactly as they do in production.",
    "`daysAgo` is relative, so a reseed always produces an inbox that looks current. Fractions are allowed - 0.25 is six hours ago.",
    "`leadStatus` is one of: new, contacted, interested, enrolled, lost.",
    "`note` lands on the activity record, never on the Person, because staff notes must not sit on a row that could be exported.",
    "None of this reaches production: convex/devSeed.ts refuses any deployment that is not local or the named hosted dev deployment (DEV_DEPLOYMENT_NAME).",
    "`books` are sample titles with an English and an Assamese edition; `bundles` group them by slug and carry a price per language in RUPEES (stored as paise). Everything here is published, marked sample, and replaced the moment the owner edits it.",
    "`orders` name a bundle slug and a language per line; the seed prices them from the bundle, exactly as checkout would. `status` is one of: awaiting_payment, paid, packed, shipped, delivered, ready_for_collection, collected, cancelled, refunded. Collection orders carry no address.",
    "`campaigns` are sample promotions, live at once and named \"Sample: …\" so a reseed replaces them."
  ],
